    "snippet": "Dec 17, 2025         The 8087 was an extremely complex chip for its time, containing somewhere between 40,000 and 75,000 transistors, depending on the source.2To explore how the 8087 works, I opened up a chip and took numerous photos of the silicon die with a microscope. Around the edges of the die, you can see the hair-thin bond wires that connect the chip to its 40 external pins.   Summarize",
