    "url": "https://specpicks.com/reviews/intel-8087-microcode-decap-news-2026",
    "title": "Inside the Intel 8087: Decapping a 1980 Math | SpecPicks",
    "snippet": "Jun 5, 2026         A volunteer reverse-engineering team has finished decapping an Intel 8087 math coprocessor from 1980 and successfully read its complete on-die microcode ROM under a microscope. The result is a window into how 1980s-era math coprocessors actually computed floating-point operations at the transistor level — and a primary-source document for the early implementation of what became the IEEE 754 floating-point standard.   Summarize",
