    "title": "The stack circuitry of the Intel 8087 floating point chip, reverse ...",
    "snippet": "A reverse-engineering deep dive examines Intel’s 8087 floating-point coprocessor, mapping its die and explaining its stack-based register file, unusual microcode ROM, and on-chip subsystems that enabled major floating-point speedups for IBM PC applications and influenced modern floating-point systems.   Summarize",
