    "snippet": "Jun 25, 2026         A reverse-engineering post dissects the 69-bit adder inside Intel’s 8087 floating-point coprocessor and shows how the chip squeezed useful floating-point hardware out of early-1980s transistor budgets. The comments added practical detail on transistor counts, timing, and why nobody bothers to build faithful FPGA versions of the 8087 today.   Summarize",
