    "url": "https://thechipletter.substack.com/p/amds-early-math-innovation",
    "title": "AMD's Early Math Innovation - by Babbage - The Chip Letter",
    "snippet": "Sep 11, 2022       First reverse engineering the Intel 8080. Then a second source for the Intel 8086.But by 1978 the 8086 had already been launched and in 1980 Intel announced the 8087 coprocessor. The 8086/7 took a different approach with dedicated floating point registers and instructions that slotted into the 8086 instruction stream. With an 8087 socket on the original IBM PC motherboard, the 8087 soon became much more popular.   Summarize",
